{"v":1,"book":"gita","n":1,"title":"Arjuna's Dilemma","hosts":[{"id":"A","name":"Emma","voice":"en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural"},{"id":"B","name":"Brian","voice":"en-US-BrianMultilingualNeural"}],"duration":603.264,"segments":[{"title":"Welcome","start":0.0},{"title":"The story","start":53.52},{"title":"Lesson 1 · Duty and emotion","start":311.616},{"title":"Lesson 2 · Face reality","start":354.168},{"title":"Lesson 3 · Doubt is honest","start":384.144},{"title":"Lesson 4 · No perfect solution","start":410.64},{"title":"Lesson 5 · Seek wisdom","start":445.728},{"title":"Lesson 6 · Your role matters","start":475.128},{"title":"Lesson 7 · Compassion and hard choices","start":508.272},{"title":"Lesson 8 · Admit what you don't know","start":535.464},{"title":"Wrap-up","start":561.696}],"turns":[{"s":"A","start":0.0,"end":3.0,"text":"Welcome to Shruti. I'm Emma.","L":[],"words":[[0.105,0.408,"Welcome"],[0.526,0.132,"to"],[0.671,0.579,"Shruti"],[1.658,0.329,"I'm"],[2.0,0.618,"Emma"]]},{"s":"B","start":3.288,"end":11.016,"text":"And I'm Brian. Today we start the Bhagavad-Gita at the very beginning: Chapter One, Arjuna's Dilemma.","L":[],"words":[[0.066,0.118,"And"],[0.197,0.184,"I'm"],[0.395,0.513,"Brian"],[1.329,0.395,"Today"],[1.737,0.118,"we"],[1.868,0.395,"start"],[2.276,0.105,"the"],[2.395,0.855,"Bhagavad-Geeta"],[3.263,0.145,"at"],[3.421,0.079,"the"],[3.513,0.329,"very"],[3.855,0.539,"beginning"],[5.079,0.487,"Chapter"],[5.579,0.434,"One"],[6.211,0.566,"Arjuna's"],[6.789,0.539,"Dilemma"]]},{"s":"A","start":11.304,"end":24.312,"text":"This is the chapter where nothing is taught yet. Nobody gives a lecture. A man simply falls apart, in front of everyone, at the worst possible moment. And that is exactly why it matters.","L":[],"words":[[0.092,0.224,"This"],[0.329,0.118,"is"],[0.461,0.118,"the"],[0.592,0.566,"chapter"],[1.171,0.158,"where"],[1.342,0.408,"nothing"],[1.763,0.145,"is"],[1.921,0.303,"taught"],[2.237,0.408,"yet"],[3.079,0.434,"Nobody"],[3.526,0.263,"gives"],[3.803,0.066,"a"],[3.882,0.592,"lecture"],[4.895,0.066,"A"],[4.974,0.342,"man"],[5.329,0.421,"simply"],[5.763,0.329,"falls"],[6.105,0.5,"apart"],[6.855,0.145,"in"],[7.013,0.303,"front"],[7.329,0.105,"of"],[7.447,0.618,"everyone"],[8.355,0.105,"at"],[8.474,0.105,"the"],[8.592,0.355,"worst"],[8.961,0.5,"possible"],[9.474,0.592,"moment"],[10.5,0.105,"And"],[10.618,0.211,"that"],[10.842,0.158,"is"],[11.013,0.579,"exactly"],[11.605,0.197,"why"],[11.816,0.118,"it"],[11.947,0.671,"matters"]]},{"s":"B","start":24.6,"end":34.824,"text":"We'll tell the whole story first, including the parts that set the scene before the Gita even begins. Then we'll walk through the eight lessons that come out of this chapter.","L":[],"words":[[0.092,0.145,"We'll"],[0.25,0.263,"tell"],[0.526,0.092,"the"],[0.632,0.224,"whole"],[0.868,0.408,"story"],[1.289,0.579,"first"],[2.079,0.513,"including"],[2.605,0.092,"the"],[2.711,0.395,"parts"],[3.118,0.171,"that"],[3.303,0.263,"set"],[3.579,0.079,"the"],[3.671,0.434,"scene"],[4.118,0.329,"before"],[4.461,0.092,"the"],[4.566,0.382,"Gita"],[4.961,0.316,"even"],[5.289,0.605,"begins"],[6.303,0.211,"Then"],[6.526,0.197,"we'll"],[6.737,0.342,"walk"],[7.092,0.224,"through"],[7.329,0.079,"the"],[7.421,0.316,"eight"],[7.75,0.526,"lessons"],[8.289,0.171,"that"],[8.474,0.237,"come"],[8.724,0.197,"out"],[8.934,0.092,"of"],[9.039,0.158,"this"],[9.211,0.618,"chapter"]]},{"s":"A","start":35.112,"end":52.656,"text":"One note before we start. The rendition we're reading, by Ramananda Prasad, keeps only the first and last verses of this chapter and gives a short summary in between. When we tell parts of the story that come from the full Gita or from the Mahabharata around it, we'll say so.","L":[],"words":[[0.092,0.197,"One"],[0.303,0.237,"note"],[0.553,0.342,"before"],[0.908,0.092,"we"],[1.013,0.566,"start"],[2.0,0.079,"The"],[2.092,0.618,"rendition"],[2.724,0.171,"we're"],[2.908,0.461,"reading"],[3.566,0.158,"by"],[3.737,0.566,"Ramananda"],[4.316,0.605,"Prasad"],[5.224,0.316,"keeps"],[5.553,0.25,"only"],[5.816,0.118,"the"],[5.947,0.408,"first"],[6.368,0.118,"and"],[6.5,0.316,"last"],[6.829,0.461,"verses"],[7.303,0.105,"of"],[7.421,0.184,"this"],[7.618,0.553,"chapter"],[8.605,0.105,"and"],[8.724,0.237,"gives"],[8.974,0.053,"a"],[9.039,0.329,"short"],[9.382,0.487,"summary"],[9.882,0.105,"in"],[10.0,0.605,"between"],[11.039,0.118,"When"],[11.171,0.118,"we"],[11.303,0.237,"tell"],[11.553,0.329,"parts"],[11.895,0.079,"of"],[11.987,0.105,"the"],[12.105,0.421,"story"],[12.539,0.184,"that"],[12.737,0.25,"come"],[13.0,0.184,"from"],[13.197,0.092,"the"],[13.303,0.276,"full"],[13.592,0.434,"Gita"],[14.118,0.145,"or"],[14.276,0.197,"from"],[14.487,0.092,"the"],[14.592,0.921,"Mahabharata"],[15.526,0.382,"around"],[15.921,0.184,"it"],[16.329,0.145,"we'll"],[16.487,0.237,"say"],[16.737,0.408,"so"]]},{"s":"B","start":53.52,"end":75.072,"text":"So, the setting. The Gita is a small part of a huge epic, the Mahabharata. Two branches of one royal family are fighting over a kingdom. On one side, the five Pandava brothers. On the other, their cousins, the hundred sons of the blind king Dhritarashtra, led by the eldest, Duryodhana.","L":[],"words":[[0.051,0.303,"So"],[0.367,0.132,"the"],[0.512,0.579,"setting"],[1.5,0.079,"The"],[1.592,0.382,"Gita"],[1.987,0.171,"is"],[2.171,0.066,"a"],[2.25,0.408,"small"],[2.671,0.342,"part"],[3.026,0.092,"of"],[3.132,0.039,"a"],[3.184,0.461,"huge"],[3.671,0.553,"epic"],[4.697,0.118,"the"],[4.829,0.961,"Mahabharata"],[6.211,0.224,"Two"],[6.447,0.605,"branches"],[7.066,0.184,"of"],[7.263,0.289,"one"],[7.566,0.303,"royal"],[7.882,0.566,"family"],[8.461,0.184,"are"],[8.658,0.461,"fighting"],[9.132,0.263,"over"],[9.408,0.053,"a"],[9.474,0.553,"kingdom"],[10.447,0.197,"On"],[10.658,0.237,"one"],[10.908,0.513,"side"],[11.447,0.118,"the"],[11.579,0.395,"five"],[11.987,0.461,"Pandava"],[12.461,0.632,"brothers"],[13.513,0.132,"On"],[13.658,0.092,"the"],[13.763,0.487,"other"],[14.553,0.25,"their"],[14.816,0.632,"cousins"],[15.474,0.092,"the"],[15.579,0.355,"hundred"],[15.947,0.434,"sons"],[16.395,0.105,"of"],[16.513,0.105,"the"],[16.632,0.408,"blind"],[17.053,0.263,"king"],[17.329,0.895,"Dhritarashtra"],[18.829,0.316,"led"],[19.158,0.158,"by"],[19.329,0.079,"the"],[19.421,0.711,"eldest"],[20.303,0.855,"Duryodhana"]]},{"s":"A","start":75.36,"end":97.776,"text":"And this is background from the Mahabharata, not from our book. The Pandavas had been cheated out of their share of the kingdom in a rigged game of dice, sent into exile for thirteen years, and when they came back and asked for their land, Duryodhana refused. They asked for just five villages. He said he wouldn't give them enough land to fit the point of a needle.","L":[],"words":[[0.105,0.118,"And"],[0.237,0.237,"this"],[0.487,0.145,"is"],[0.645,0.632,"background"],[1.289,0.184,"from"],[1.487,0.092,"the"],[1.592,0.961,"Mahabharata"],[2.868,0.224,"not"],[3.105,0.211,"from"],[3.329,0.145,"our"],[3.487,0.461,"book"],[4.382,0.079,"The"],[4.474,0.645,"Pandavas"],[5.132,0.145,"had"],[5.289,0.171,"been"],[5.474,0.395,"cheated"],[5.882,0.171,"out"],[6.066,0.079,"of"],[6.158,0.158,"their"],[6.329,0.263,"share"],[6.605,0.092,"of"],[6.711,0.105,"the"],[6.829,0.434,"kingdom"],[7.276,0.092,"in"],[7.382,0.066,"a"],[7.461,0.289,"rigged"],[7.763,0.237,"game"],[8.013,0.132,"of"],[8.158,0.461,"dice"],[9.145,0.263,"sent"],[9.421,0.224,"into"],[9.658,0.513,"exile"],[10.184,0.158,"for"],[10.355,0.5,"thirteen"],[10.868,0.447,"years"],[11.658,0.145,"and"],[11.816,0.132,"when"],[11.961,0.132,"they"],[12.105,0.289,"came"],[12.408,0.303,"back"],[12.724,0.118,"and"],[12.855,0.289,"asked"],[13.158,0.118,"for"],[13.289,0.184,"their"],[13.487,0.421,"land"],[14.184,0.724,"Duryodhana"],[14.921,0.763,"refused"],[16.105,0.145,"They"],[16.263,0.329,"asked"],[16.605,0.145,"for"],[16.763,0.25,"just"],[17.026,0.25,"five"],[17.289,0.789,"villages"],[18.605,0.118,"He"],[18.737,0.224,"said"],[18.974,0.132,"he"],[19.118,0.303,"wouldn't"],[19.434,0.171,"give"],[19.618,0.158,"them"],[19.789,0.355,"enough"],[20.158,0.355,"land"],[20.526,0.092,"to"],[20.632,0.237,"fit"],[20.882,0.105,"the"],[21.0,0.329,"point"],[21.342,0.079,"of"],[21.434,0.053,"a"],[21.5,0.526,"needle"]]},{"s":"B","start":98.064,"end":119.52,"text":"So war became unavoidable. Two enormous armies gather on the plain of Kurukshetra. And here's the clever framing: the whole Gita is told as a report. The blind king can't see the battlefield, so his charioteer, Sanjaya, who has been given the gift of seeing far-off events, describes it to him.","L":[],"words":[[0.051,0.211,"So"],[0.275,0.355,"war"],[0.643,0.526,"became"],[1.196,0.921,"unavoidable"],[2.539,0.303,"Two"],[2.855,0.605,"enormous"],[3.474,0.447,"armies"],[3.934,0.539,"gather"],[4.487,0.158,"on"],[4.658,0.092,"the"],[4.763,0.395,"plain"],[5.171,0.132,"of"],[5.316,0.855,"Kurukshetra"],[6.592,0.105,"And"],[6.711,0.368,"here's"],[7.092,0.105,"the"],[7.211,0.382,"clever"],[7.605,0.592,"framing"],[8.803,0.105,"the"],[8.921,0.263,"whole"],[9.197,0.355,"Gita"],[9.566,0.211,"is"],[9.789,0.434,"told"],[10.237,0.145,"as"],[10.395,0.066,"a"],[10.474,0.618,"report"],[11.513,0.079,"The"],[11.605,0.382,"blind"],[12.0,0.342,"king"],[12.355,0.289,"can't"],[12.658,0.237,"see"],[12.908,0.092,"the"],[13.013,0.711,"battlefield"],[14.132,0.184,"so"],[14.329,0.158,"his"],[14.5,0.842,"charioteer"],[15.645,0.737,"Sanjaya"],[16.908,0.132,"who"],[17.053,0.145,"has"],[17.211,0.158,"been"],[17.382,0.263,"given"],[17.658,0.092,"the"],[17.763,0.368,"gift"],[18.145,0.092,"of"],[18.25,0.316,"seeing"],[18.579,0.474,"far-off"],[19.066,0.5,"events"],[19.974,0.553,"describes"],[20.539,0.092,"it"],[20.645,0.105,"to"],[20.763,0.303,"him"]]},{"s":"A","start":119.808,"end":133.68,"text":"That's the first verse in our book, verse one point one. The blind King inquired from his charioteer: O Sanjaya, tell me in detail, what did my sons and the Pandavas do in the battlefield before the war started?","L":[],"words":[[0.105,0.237,"That's"],[0.355,0.105,"the"],